00:25:47.731 --> 00:25:50.367
>> alan built a network of

00:25:50.367 --> 00:25:50.934
friends who shared his

00:25:50.934 --> 00:25:51.702
intellectual passions.

00:25:51.702 --> 00:25:53.871
Among them were rebecca solnit,

00:25:53.871 --> 00:25:54.572
whose literary explorations of

00:25:54.572 --> 00:25:55.206
place and identity resonated

00:25:55.206 --> 00:25:57.206
with alan's architectural

00:25:57.875 --> 00:25:58.609
philosophy.

00:25:58.609 --> 00:25:59.310
And professor robert cherney,

00:25:59.310 --> 00:26:01.212
whose academic insights on

00:26:01.212 --> 00:26:01.979
history and politics

00:26:01.979 --> 00:26:02.413
complemented alan's thoughts on

00:26:02.413 --> 00:26:04.413
preservation.

00:26:05.516 --> 00:26:06.830
His best friend ed kindred

00:26:06.830 --> 00:26:06.751
spirit was his closest

00:26:06.751 --> 00:26:08.751
confidant accompanying him

00:26:09.353 --> 00:26:10.870
in journeys both literal

00:26:10.870 --> 00:26:10.788
and philosophical where the two

00:26:10.788 --> 00:26:13.188
often delved into profound

00:26:13.658 --> 00:26:14.426
discussions about humanity, art

00:26:14.426 --> 00:26:14.859
and the evolving narratives of

00:26:14.859 --> 00:26:16.859
urban spaces.

00:26:17.829 --> 00:26:18.596
Alan martinez was not only a

00:26:18.596 --> 00:26:19.364
dedicated professional he was a

00:26:19.364 --> 00:26:21.764
compassionate individual with a

00:26:21.766 --> 00:26:22.199
deep love for history

00:26:22.199 --> 00:26:22.900
and humanity.

00:26:22.900 --> 00:26:25.300
